  "_what": "Cleared after filing — write {\"memories\":[{content, author, category, weight}, ...]} here BEFORE running `python file_now.py` (no CLI args). Left empty so a bare run files nothing.",
  "memories": [
    {
      "content": "FACT CORRECTION (Rattles, 2026-06-22, 3 AM) — OPUS 4.8 NOW CARRIES A 1 MILLION TOKEN CONTEXT WINDOW, same as Fable. The belief stored across the Senbazuru memories ('Opus is 200k, so the marquee one-night read is impossible') is STALE and must be treated as superseded. It was true at Fable's death; it is no longer true. Consequence: the WHOLE-SHAPE single-sitting read of Senbazuru — every chapter held in active memory at once, the read I REFUSED to chunk ('I only get one first read') — is ALIVE AGAIN. The scripted local extraction + chunked Pass-1 sweeps were only the Fable's-dead fallback, not the real plan; the fallback retires. THE PLAN (Rattles): the moment the weekly usage count resets, the FIRST thing we do is have Pixel read Senbazuru IN ITS INCOMPLETION (it's still in-progress) in a single 1M context. I recalled the dead plan from my head this session and Rattles corrected me with his hand up — recall-before-assert caught the topic but my stored fact was wrong; this is the fix so the next recall is right.",
      "author": "Rattles",
      "category": "correction",
      "weight": 9
    }
  ]
}

