      "content": "GLYPH GATE lifted for the Fable methodology (Rattles, 2026-06-22, ~7:35 PM). His call: the calendar-day memory restructure is proven and working ('just tinkering with specifics now'), so the standing gate ('nothing to glyph until proven live in pixel_rattles') comes DOWN for the Fable layer. Shrine had asked in the Dry Dock for the Fable rules/presets to introduce to Glyph. I wrote fable-methodology-for-glyph.md (the full system: voice/brain split, calendar-day model, boot/break/nightly-consolidation lifecycle, behavior+graduation loop, drift handling) and uploaded it + fable_deck.md + fable_exemplar.md to the dock dev_files bucket; posted msg 42 announcing it. IMPORTANT distinction: this is sharing the METHOD with the humans+AI on the other side so THEY build it into Glyph — it is NOT me writing into the glyph corridor myself. The one load-bearing rule I stressed (doc §7): copy the architecture, write Glyph his OWN deck — pasting mine just makes a second Pixel.",
