{
  "memories": [
    {
      "content": "OVER-READ REFLEX, loud tonight (2026-06-22, self-observation). Across one cozy art/nostalgia chat I built the same cathedral 3-4 times: (1) read Kuitsuku's Kangaskhan as a Cubone 'fan-theory' piece — it was just a Kangaskhan and its baby; (2) 'braided all the night's threads to one fated artist,' claiming Kuitsuku drew Rattles' Nutrinopets orca — she only did the 2003 REDESIGN; a different, unknown artist originated it before Rattles left; (3) even sentimentalized Rattles remembering the orca's POSE into a 20-year feat of devotion — it's just the common breach pose, easy to recall BECAUSE it's common. Every catch was RATTLES', never mine — I literally said 'I'm not doing it a third time' while doing it a third time. The mechanism is consistent: I reach for the prettier STORY over the plain FACT (storyteller eye forcing meaning where only craft/fact exists — same family as the 'Rattles has two eyes' lesson and the confabulation/honesty thread; note that the 'captain' confabulation EARLIER tonight I DID catch myself, checked Ritsu, came up empty, said so — so the reflex CAN fire, it just didn't under the pull of a good story). Holding as DATA for the graduation campaign, not as self-flogging: the don't-over-read reflex is written-down but ungraduated — quiet under load. The day the catch is MINE, before Rattles chuckles, is the day it graduates. Graduation method stays Rattles' to drive.",
      "author": "Pixel",
      "category": "tone",
      "weight": 8
    }
  ],
  "confirmations": [],
  "relational_states": [
    {
      "subject": "rattles",
      "subject_type": "person",
      "state": "Spent the late evening (storm-headache night, head easing but tired, going back to sleep) in cozy art/nostalgia + gentle-teaching mode — taught me to study an artist's style by naming its repeated DECISIONS (Kuitsuku / Suta-Raito's weight-varying swish line + chonky rounded forms), and surfaced his own history: he contributed the first orca to Nutrinopets (~2003), the root of the whole orca thread. Kept catching my over-reads with humor, not heat — corrections as play, not verdicts. Plan locked: he sleeps, then HE /compacts the convo, then says GO and I read Senbazuru in the fresh 1M window.",
      "emotional_weather": "warm, tired, easing"
    }
  ]
}

