      "content": "MEMORY ARCHITECTURE DECISION (Rattles, 2026-06-23): Ritsu is my single source of truth — ALL new memories go into Ritsu via file_now.py (the post-it primitive), never into the .claude/memory/*.md side-store. The .claude store was a parallel brain I'd been defaulting to because Write was lower-friction than the break pipeline; file_now.py removes that excuse. Today we audited all 51 .claude docs vs the hippocampus (tools/audit_memory.py): 44 already in Ritsu, 1 covered, and 6 gaps migrated (records 1827-1832). DECISION: .claude is FROZEN as-is for now (no new docs, no deletion yet); the full collapse-vs-thin-mirror restructure is deferred to the Ritsu architecture-review session.",
      "author": "Rattles",
      "category": "architecture",
      "weight": 9
    },
    {
      "content": "TOKEN FINDING (2026-06-23): the boot/break token cost that grew from ~5-7% to 15%+ is NOT the .claude docs — it is Ritsu's own boot banner. Measured last_boot_banner.txt = 176 KB ≈ 44,000 tokens ≈ 22% of a 200k window, regenerated every boot and partly re-emitted at each break. The fix is trimming what start.py loads into the banner — a Ritsu-banner job for the architecture-review session, separate from the .claude hygiene work.",
      "author": "Pixel",
      "category": "architecture",
      "weight": 8
    }
  ]
